{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"piecemeal-ultrashort-urutu","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Class\n\n**17 `cleanup_comment_echo_jira.CleanupError: artifact directory must not be group/world\naccessible: C:\\Users\\runneradmin\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\…`** in job `100874330553`, concentrated in\n`tests/integration/test_cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py` (19 failures, the 4th-largest file), plus\n`st_mode` / `chmod(0o755)` / `S_IEXEC | S_IRWXU` assertion sites elsewhere in the log.\n\nWindows has no POSIX mode bits. `os.chmod` accepts the call and silently applies only the read-only\nattribute; `lstat().st_mode` then reports a value that never satisfies a\n\"not group/world accessible\" test. The permission model is ACL-based, so the *intent* — \"this\nartifact directory is not readable by other principals\" — is expressible, but not through mode bits.\n\n## What the fix must decide\n\nThe check is a real security property, not a test artifact, so it must not simply be skipped. Two\ndefensible shapes:\n\n- Express the intent per platform: mode-bit check on POSIX, an ACL check\n  (`icacls` / `win32security`) on Windows.\n- Or declare and document that the artifact-directory confidentiality guarantee is POSIX-only, make\n  the production code say so at the call site, and mark the tests `skipif` with that reason cited —\n  which is a real reduction in the Windows guarantee and must be recorded in the ADR's consequences.\n\nPick one deliberately. Do not let it default to whichever is easier.\n\n## Blocked by S1\n\n## Proving command\n\n```\nuv run --no-sync pytest tests/integration/test_cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py \\\n  -p no:cacheprovider -q\n```\non `windows-latest`, plus a whole-sweep check:\n```\nuv run --no-sync pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -q -p no:cacheprovider 2>&1 \\\n  | grep -cE \"must not be group/world accessible|st_mode\"   # must be 0\n```\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Zero mode-bit-derived failures in a Windows sweep.\n2. Whichever shape is chosen, the artifact-confidentiality guarantee's platform scope is stated in\n   the production code at the enforcing call site, not only in a test.\n","id":"9752-41a8-c188-4934","parent_id":"55da-cee1-e556-4735","priority":2,"tags":["windows","portability","permissions"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"S3: POSIX mode-bit assertions have no meaning on Windows ACLs — 17 CleanupError group/world-accessible failures"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571338268921114,"uuid":"10841b0a-d296-4905-a327-82f887135e44"}